# Revisions that changed formatting only, and that `git blame` should look
# through rather than at. A commit belongs here when it rewrote many lines
# without changing what any of them do -- a whole-tree linter autocorrect, a
# formatter adoption -- so that blame keeps pointing at whoever last changed
# the MEANING of a line instead of at the sweep that reindented it.
#
# This file does nothing on its own. Git only consults it when told to, so each
# clone opts in once, locally:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# GitHub reads it automatically for blame views in the web UI; `git blame` on
# the command line does not until you run that config line. A stale or
# mistyped SHA makes blame fail outright ("no such commit"), so only add SHAs
# that exist on main, and only after the commit has actually landed.
#
# Entries are newest last. Keep the comment above each one.

